export anchor XeroxZineStyle:
    number: 155
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Xerox zine
    idea: A photocopied punk zine spread, stapled down the middle, with ransom-note cut-out letters, typewritten listings and nothing but toner black on white paper.
    base: light
    palette:
        paperWhite: #ffffff, pages, cut-outs and fields
        toner: #0d0d0d, all text, bars, solid blocks and the primary button
        smudge: #4a4a4a, speckle and halftone texture only
        wash: #e6e6e6, grey cut-out letters and the focus fill
        desk: #c9c9c6, the surface under the zine and the tape strips
        staple: #8a8f94, staples on the fold, decorative
    type:
        Four stacks mixed like cut-outs. Headings and numbers use Impact,
        Haettenschweiler, Arial Narrow Bold, Franklin Gothic Heavy,
        sans-serif, with 64px numbers, 32px section heads and 20px
        buttons. Project names use Arial Black at 19px caps. Asides use
        Times New Roman italic at 15 to 20px. Body and labels use Courier
        New, Courier, Nimbus Mono PS, monospace at 16px with 1.45 line
        height, labels 13px bold caps. The greeting is a ransom note, each
        word on its own boxed scrap in a different stack, rotated 2 to 5
        degrees.
    layout:
        A white two page spread on a speckled grey desk with a dashed fold
        down the middle and two grey staples on it. The left page has the
        masthead, a black rotated Brightwork block and an issue note, nav
        as boxed typewriter tabs tilted alternately with Home inverted,
        then search as an underline, New project, a BELL count button and
        the name. Below come a black date strip, the ransom note greeting,
        a black splat with a bang beside the scrawled overdue line, four
        taped cut-out boxes in a two by two grid with the overdue one
        inverted, and a scene report list with black time tags floated
        right. The right page holds a numbered track listing of the six
        projects with big 01 to 06 numerals, caps names, a status box, and
        a meta line with a hatched bar and the facts, then the tally chart
        with dotted halftone bars for last week and solid bars for this
        week. Small page folios sit at the foot. Below 900px the pages
        stack and the staples hide.
    spacing: Loose 4px base, mostly 8, 12, 18 and 32. Pages have 36px margins like a folded A5 sheet.
    density: Packed and lumpy. Listings are tight, cut-outs float with uneven gaps.
    corners: Square everywhere. Scraps are rotated rather than rounded.
    borders: Solid toner lines from 2 to 4px. Dashed lines for the fold and soft dividers.
    shadows: Only the spread sits on the desk with a flat 6px grey offset. Speckle gradients fake copier noise.
    icons:
        Hand drawn feel in toner. A wobbly circled tick means On track, an
        outline triangle with a bang means At risk, a solid black box with
        an X means Behind, and a black splat with a bang marks overdue.
    focus: A 3px dashed toner outline offset 4px, with a wash fill on fields and rows.
    tone: Blunt lower case asides and shouted caps, such as scene report, track listing and deal with it today.
